Provenance and licensing
========================

What this is
------------

Research work on the Atmel AT89C51RD2 / AT89C51ED2 for reverse engineering: a device-model and
peripheral build-out on top of ucsim, a verification bed of 26 counted suites plus runtests
(reported, never counted), and the analysis notes that record what the datasheet actually says.
Distributed under GPL-2.0-or-later (see LICENSE), the same licence as ucsim, because the code here
modifies and extends ucsim.

The simulator base
------------------

Base tree: `CrispStrobe/ucsim-stc`, commit
`441710c87dc93577caf1c64394eefb86b928eee2` (that commit is `origin/master`). It is NOT
redistributed here. To reproduce the exact tree every suite in `t/` was run against:

    git clone https://github.com/CrispStrobe/ucsim-stc vendor/ucsim-stc
    git -C vendor/ucsim-stc checkout 441710c
    git -C vendor/ucsim-stc apply ../patches/rd2-vs-ucsim-stc-441710c.patch
    # the ../ is needed: `git -C` resolves the patch path against the target directory
    ./build.sh

The patch touches **38 files**: 28 modified (+2494 / -192, measured 2026-11-14) and 10 added
(`rd2_boot`, `rd2_brg`, `rd2_eeprom`, `rd2_kbd`, `rd2_spi` and their `*cl.h`, 2483 lines). Four
files the working tree also
changes are deliberately left out — `ucsim/src/common.mk`, `ucsim/src/packages.mk`,
`ucsim/src/core/utils.src/ddconfig.h`, `ucsim/docs/Makefile` — because they are `./configure` output
and the copies in the base tree record one machine (curses and flex detected off, an install prefix
pointed at the author's home). `build.sh` runs `configure` after the patch, so every reader gets
their own values. It was verified by applying the patch to a fresh clone of that commit and
comparing trees: file-by-file comparison of all 38 patched paths reports no content difference at
all, and the only other differences under `ucsim/src` are build artefacts. `slices/` holds the two
changes cut as self-contained, upstream-sized pieces -- the timer-2 `cycles` bug and the
port-mirror double-notify -- each with its own patch, text and evidence.

Attribution note: the 10 new files carry `Copyright (C) 2026 Oleksiy`. The fork's own new files
(`stc12_*.cc`) carry `Copyright (C) 2026 CrispStrobe`; that header convention was copied, the
authorship is not theirs.

Datasheets are not included
---------------------------

`doc4235` (AT89C51RD2 datasheet) and `doc4316` (Atmel C51 Hardware Manual) are Atmel/Microchip
copyrighted documents and are not redistributed here. The analysis documents cite them by section
and by PRINTED page number (the datasheet's own numbering, which is offset from the PDF page
index); no page text is reproduced at length. Obtain the PDFs from Microchip.

Third-party trees referenced but not redistributed
--------------------------------------------------

    vendor/ucsim-stc/   the simulator (GPL-2.0-or-later) -- recipe above
    vendor/cpu8051/     Simon Kuhn's independent C ISS, used as a third opinion
    vendor/mcs51-rs/    Rust mcs51 assembler/linker/sim; `xval/Cargo.toml` path-deps expect it
                        at vendor/mcs51-rs, so `cargo build` in xval/ needs that clone first
    xval/               MY one-file driver that runs an image on the Rust i8051 core and prints
                        a diffable trace; published here as source only (target/ excluded)

Ghidra side lives elsewhere
---------------------------

The AT89C51RD2 Ghidra language is a separate repo, `ghidra-at89c51rd2` (Apache-2.0, because
`rd2.sinc` is a derivative of Ghidra's `8051_main.sinc`), together with `langbuild`, `gh51` and
the Ghidra scripts in `gh/`. The gated patch to Ghidra's shared include is
`ghidra-8051-dual-dptr` (Apache-2.0). `t/langtest.py`, `t/rmwtest.py`, `t/banktest.py` and
`t/symmaptest.py` are the Ghidra-side suites kept here for completeness of the bed; all four
need that language installed via `langbuild` first. `langtest`, `rmwtest` and `symmaptest` are
deliberately outside `t/floor.sh` because each starts a headless Ghidra; `banktest` runs inside
the floor's counted set. `symmaptest` ships here rather than beside the language because half of
it is the simulator: it gives one `.sym` to ucsim's `sym` command and the same bytes to
`gh/LoadSym51.java`. `gh/` is duplicated in the language repo so each repo runs on its own,
except `LoadSym51.java`, which lives only here for that same reason.
